;; D31's fixture: a shaft of one-way ledges that span it wall to wall. A held
;; jump (3.25 tiles) goes up through each three-row step, so the top is
;; reached; the only way back down is through the ledges (nothing to walk
;; off, the walls smooth and five apart), so the way back needs the drop
;; (down and jump). Without drop-through the top is a trap.
(fixture
  name: "a shaft of ledges, up by jumps and down only by dropping through"
  expect: reachable
  why: "the envelope (3-tile rises) and D31's drop-through"
  start: (12 8)
  target: ((12 2) (12 5))
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "#########     ###########"
   "#########     ###########"
   "#########=====###########"
   "#########     ###########"
   "#########     ###########"
   "#########=====###########"
   "#########     ###########"
   "#########     ###########"
   "#########################"
   "#########################"))
